        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edward Burne-Jones, William Morris\n- Products: The Beguiling of Merlin\n- Organizations: Morris, Marshall, Faulkner & Co.\n- Concepts: Pre-Raphaelite movement, decorative arts\n- Roles: British artist, designer, founding partner\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Burne-Jones was born on 28 August 1833 and died on 17 June 1898.\n- Edward Burne-Jones was a British artist and designer associated with the later phase of the Pre-Raphaelite movement.\n- Edward Burne-Jones worked closely with William Morris on a wide range of decorative arts.\n- Edward Burne-Jones was a founding partner in Morris, Marshall, Faulkner & Co.\n- The Beguiling of Merlin is a painting by the Pre-Raphaelite painter Edward Burne-Jones.\n- Edward Burne-Jones created The Beguiling of Merlin between 1872 and 1877.",
